WEBVTT

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:04.480
<i>The year is 2205 A.D.</i>

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:14.020
<i>To annihilate the History Retrograde 
Army, who scheme to alter history,</i>

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:17.150
<i>we, who were born from swords,</i>

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.480
<i>engage in mortal combat today as well!</i>

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.750
<i>That's not that cool, is it?</i>

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.370
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.400
"This anime is about the 
stories of the Hanamaru days

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:04.250
of a certain group of Sword 
Warriors in a certain citadel."

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.240
Finally...

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:24.320
Please let me know the moment you need me.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.830
You're being too noisy!

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:27.930
Hey!

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.860
Master!

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:32.160
I handled it myself.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:34.760
In four hours, one of them will appear!

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:36.220
Wh-What?

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.370
Finished.

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:47.020
It looks pretty nice.

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:48.080
What do you think?

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:49.640
It's cute, isn't it?

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:53.270
Hey. You can compliment me 
more specifically, can't you?

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:58.900
Don't my nails look a little different than usual?

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.980
The color... is different!

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:03.860
Yes, that's right.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:06.920
This kind of effort is necessary,

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:09.570
if Master is going to use me more.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.620
Because you're making yourself cute?

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:13.970
Of course it is.

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:17.450
Even you must prefer cute things 
over non-cute things, right?

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:21.250
That's why I was the first one 
to step foot in this citadel.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.290
I'm grateful to Master for that.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:25.990
But,

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:30.510
I might not be loved by 
Master for much longer.

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:32.090
Why?

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.820
So, what did you want to discuss?

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.040
When you invite me to join you for a bath,

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.840
you usually want to talk
about something, don't you?

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.880
The dinner menu? I think omelet rice—

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:48.540
That's not why.

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:51.550
I'm not worried about the dinner menu today.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.520
It's about Kara-chan,
who joined us last week.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:00.830
Ookurikara?

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.090
33 - Tachi
 <b>Ookurikara</b>

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:03.790
I don't plan to make friends.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:07.290
That's true.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:11.340
No one's going to get near
 Kara-bou if he's got that attitude.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:13.990
Hopefully something changes his mind.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:22.770
It's raining?

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.980
It's really coming down.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:31.090
It's a shame that we have to hang these 
up indoors, where they won't dry well.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:33.750
It's because there's still 
a lot of unwashed clothes.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:37.950
If anyone is dispatched today, they'll just 
have to go out in half-dried clothes.

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:40.330
Half-dried clothes would be troublesome.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:42.170
Then why don't we all have some tea?

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:44.650
Well, should we just go borrow from someone?

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.220
Battle clothes?

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:49.080
Are you okay with wearing 
something that isn't yours?

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:52.710
I'd make it work if they fit.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:57.110
All right, let's go search for someone 
with lots of battle clothes.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.650
Hey, are you leaving without 
putting these up to dry?

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:02.600
My pride and joy!

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:06.020
I have tons of Aizen Myouou T-shirts!

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:15.560
You've made Aizen Myouou fat!

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:17.430
Who was that?

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:19.350
I heard a ripping sound just now!

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.880
My body is pretty big,

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.750
so I guess that might happen.

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:28.780
He can't fight like this.

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:30.350
He looks like a little kid.

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:33.990
I told them to stop.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:36.800
I told them I wouldn't go along with it.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.570
I'm sorry, Shokudaikiri.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:44.750
Oh, there's so many, Nakigitsune.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:46.650
Why are there so many?

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:49.300
You can feel his fastidiousness.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:52.020
Ah, don't just go touching them!

00:05:57.970 --> 00:05:59.200
I see now.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:02.960
This makes us look exactly like male 
employees of a service restaurant.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.940
Male employees of a service restaurant?

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.250
What's that?

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:12.550
It was written about in a book called a 
"magazine" that I received from Master once.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:15.080
They were called hos-something-or-other.

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:18.170
But, I recall that they worked 
at a service restaurant.

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:22.690
Kasen-kun?

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:26.890
Please let me explain.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:34.400
So, exactly what kind of shop is it?

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.170
I believe they specialize in hospitality.

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:37.450
Hospitality?

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:41.480
It was a friendly shop providing 
enjoyable hospitality for its guests.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:42.450
Most likely.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:44.310
A friendly shop?

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:47.130
I'd love to take him to a shop like that.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:48.120
Who?

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:49.750
Kara-chan.

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:51.750
Ookurikara?

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.040
Ookurikara-dono?

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:54.790
Ookurikara?

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:57.590
That's a good idea.

00:06:57.590 --> 00:07:01.330
He's being difficult, as you all have noticed.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:02.760
I want him to get along with us.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:04.920
That's a bit...

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:07.020
I'll be taking back my clothes, then.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:08.840
D'oh...

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:10.860
Apparently they've become
rather fond of those clothes...

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.430
Why don't we at least give it a shot?

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:16.370
We'll provide hospitality 
to Ookurikara as these

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:18.520
male employees at the service whatever.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:19.990
Understood.

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:20.740
Fine.

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:22.770
Are tea and dumplings acceptable?

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:24.880
If Shokudaikiri insists.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:27.710
I'm pretty confident in 
my hospitality abilities.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:29.100
Thank you.

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:32.260
If that's settled, then 
it's time to get ready.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:40.800
Hospitality.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:47.420
What should I do?

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:49.930
Don't worry about me.

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:50.980
Come on now.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.320
Welcome!

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:17.050
Is this torture?

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:20.200
We'll start with this.

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:23.840
What is this?

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:28.060
Just try to imagine what 
kind of flower is blooming.

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:31.020
Wha?

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:32.500
Uh...

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:37.270
Well, this is something that Sen no Rikyuu
did, and it was praised as incredibly elegant.

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:40.270
Rikyuu-dono got a lot of praise for it...

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:43.450
<i>Maybe this elegance was too soon for them.</i>

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:46.000
<i>I feel as though I've failed.</i>

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:52.960
My former master was one of many 
disciples of Sen no Rikyuu.

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:55.060
Forget about what just happened.

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:58.930
I'd like for you to drink 
some genuine green tea.

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:05.340
Not you.

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:09.310
Lord Nobunaga was also 
a master of hospitality.

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:13.360
He would give his guests 
rare and unusual fruits.

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:17.030
Now, be sure to eat up.

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:17.990
It's so thin!

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:26.210
Now then, it's my turn.

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:36.210
<i>I thought I'd provide hospitality 
with a lively conversation.</i>

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:45.810
<b>Lively Conversation</b>

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:45.810
<b>Hospitality</b>

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:39.500
<i>But what are they expecting 
from a copy like me?</i>

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:45.810
<b>Copy Like Me</b>

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:45.810
<b>Expecting</b>

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:42.030
<i>But I have to say something.</i>

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:43.670
<i>A lively conversation!</i>

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:45.810
<i>No, it wouldn't matter if I spoke.</i>

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:48.130
Hey, what's the matter?

00:09:53.930 --> 00:09:57.340
Providing hospitality is my responsibility.

00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:59.370
Do you dislike foxes?

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:00.020
Foxes?

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:03.850
Animals have healing abilities, you know.

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:07.780
It's not bad.

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:11.970
This sound...

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:20.490
I'm sorry that it wasn't exactly a song.

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:23.470
Lord Date Masamune's wife, Mego-hime,

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:26.000
apparently used to play 
the koto quite often.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:30.600
This sound...

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:34.880
I remember it.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:36.900
It was a kind sound.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:39.030
He smiled.

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:39.800
He did.

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:51.490
Lord... Masamune?

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:01.450
A person without knowledge of 
cooking is the owner of a poor heart.

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:07.330
Food that has been lovingly 
prepared by one's own hands

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:10.180
is the best form of hospitality.

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:19.110
I see.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:22.380
So this is what it tastes like.

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:28.650
Let me try some, too.

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:30.030
Me, too.

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:31.200
There's plenty for everyone.

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:41.490
Not bad.

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:46.740
Delicious.

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:53.010
Kara-chan, shall we talk about the past?

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:01.690
When I think of Lord Masamune... 
do you remember, Kara-chan?

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:03.950
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:14.200
Sh-Shishiou!

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:20.970
Master!

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:22.340
He's finally here!

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:29.220
Bring more alcohol!

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:35.690
<i>He's gonna be pissed.</i>

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:38.390
Okay, Hasebe-kun, you see this is...

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:40.100
He's here.

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:42.170
"He?"

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:45.390
He's not there.

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:46.110
What?

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:48.610
I told them to show him to Master's room.

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:07.510
It just cleared up.

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:08.920
Is that so?

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:10.630
What is that tree?

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:13.200
Did you find him?

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:14.310
No.

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:17.600
Who are we even looking for?

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:21.200
Uguisumaru, who are you talking to?

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:24.780
Ah, we just became tea-drinking friends.

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:30.480
Me?

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:34.290
34 - Tachi
 

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:34.290
My name is Mikazuki Munechika.

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:36.590
Pleased to meet you.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:38.600
Mikazuki?

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:43.510
The rarest of rare swords in all of history.

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:46.760
It's said that the most beautiful
of the Five Great Swords of Japan

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:48.800
is Mikazuki Munechika.

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:53.020
He doesn't seem like it, though.

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:55.520
He seems kind of like an old man.

00:13:57.430 --> 00:14:00.080
Probably because I was forged 
at the end of the 11th century.

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:01.990
I am indeed an old man.

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:05.030
Oh, one of the Sanjou swords 
has finally appeared?

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:07.650
I am a Gojou sword, Tsurumaru Kuninaga.

00:14:08.010 --> 00:14:10.660
Oh! Tsurumaru?

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:12.750
This place is called the Citadel.

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:16.360
It's pretty big. I'll be sure 
to show you around later.

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:20.790
Forgive my delay,
but I am called Uguisumaru.

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:23.870
Mikazuki, did you happen
to see Ookanehira anywhere?

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:26.990
I have met Heshikiri Hasebe and Shishiou.

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:31.330
So, why is it that everyone 
is wearing those clothes?

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:37.690
Our master has been hoping that Mikazuki 
Munechika would arrive for quite some time.

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:38.920
Is that so?

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:41.520
I'm sure they're happy right now.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.010
That's wonderful, isn't it?

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:46.080
Jeez, you're a simple one, aren't you?

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:50.900
Now that Mikazuki's here,
we might not be loved anymore.

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:55.300
I don't know for sure, though.

00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:58.960
All right, get a move on!

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:02.820
Ta-da! Dispatch orders!

00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:02.450
<b>Sa</b>

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:03.890
Dispatch?

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:06.000
That's quite sudden.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:07.340
I'm going to read it.

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:12.180
Captain is tachi: Mikazuki Munechika!

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:12.180
<b>Sa</b>

00:15:13.130 --> 00:15:15.790
He just got here,
and he's already made captain?

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:19.610
Next, we have uchigatana: Kashuu Kiyomitsu!

00:15:19.610 --> 00:15:21.190
Eh? Me?

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:23.410
Tantou: Gokotai!

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:24.600
That's it!

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:31.780
You called, Shishiou-san?

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:33.640
Gokotai, you're being dispatched.

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:35.020
O-Okay.

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:36.480
Let's see...

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:41.270
You are being dispatched to 
Utsunomiya Castle in 1868.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:47.650
The History Retrograde Army has infiltrated 
the Battle of Utsunomiya Castle again?

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:50.550
They seem to be trying to change 
history by intruding on the fight

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:53.300
between the former shogunate's army 
and the new government's army.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:57.290
The History Retrograde Army in that 
area isn't too strong, though, right?

00:15:57.290 --> 00:15:58.780
We've beaten them dozens of times.

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:00.820
But why them?

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:04.280
As usual, we don't know 
what Master is thinking.

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:07.090
Okay, okay! Go on and get ready.

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:09.100
You're being dispatched in 30 minutes.

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:10.150
Do your best!

00:16:10.270 --> 00:16:13.440
It's Utsunomiya Castle again. 
Piece of cake, right?

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:23.260
<i>Master definitely loves Mikazuki.</i>

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:29.050
<i>Surely, they want him to get stronger and 
become a main fighter for this citadel.</i>

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:32.840
<i>I'm the support.</i>

00:16:34.190 --> 00:16:36.010
<i>The back-up captain, if I had to guess.</i>

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:40.370
<i>Gokotai hasn't been dispatched recently,</i>

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:43.720
<i>so perhaps they're trying
to get him used to battle again?</i>

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:47.440
Let's hurry up and get this over—

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:48.680
I'm sorry for the wait.

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:59.310
Mikazuki-san, you look so cool!

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:01.860
It's from Master. Take it with you.

00:17:02.070 --> 00:17:03.380
What is this?

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:04.500
It's a protection charm.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:07.030
If something happens,
this will protect your body.

00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:09.630
Is that so? I will treasure it.

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:15.150
It's your first battle, so there's 
still a great deal you don't know.

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:17.560
Be sure to ask Kashuu any questions.

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:19.000
Yes, understood.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:20.970
Kashuu, thank you in 
advance for your support.

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:22.450
Yeah, yeah.

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:24.590
First, you operate that thing over there.

00:17:25.240 --> 00:17:27.390
It's fine, I'll do it.

00:17:30.370 --> 00:17:33.070
Date, time, location.

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:36.110
Now, let's get going.

00:17:36.510 --> 00:17:37.610
Kiyomitsu...

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:39.420
Be careful.

00:17:55.730 --> 00:17:58.880
Ho, ho! So this is Utsunomiya Castle?

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:01.110
What a splendid castle.

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:04.730
Captain, first we scout and come 
up with a battle strategy.

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:06.960
Scouting? Very well.

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:19.580
Mikazuki, there was a gate over 
there. Let's start from there.

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:22.870
Th-The enemy has appeared!

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:25.800
Well, now.

00:18:26.760 --> 00:18:27.660
Kashuu?

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:33.720
Well done, well done!

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:37.660
<i>I've been training with 
Yasusada every morning,</i>

00:18:37.830 --> 00:18:39.520
<i>so this is a piece of cake.</i>

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:45.720
Gokotai!

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:48.140
This is bad, if he gets struck again...

00:18:55.340 --> 00:18:56.310
Mikazuki!

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:14.250
This is no time to be laughing, is it?

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:26.920
I'm burning up.

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:29.600
Time to get serious, I suppose.

00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:47.080
<i>How the hell am I the back-up captain?</i>

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.480
<i>Mikazuki Munechika is in a class by himself.</i>

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:03.670
I wonder if that was the goal 
of Master's dispatch orders.

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:04.470
Huh?

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:07.070
I was overconfident in my own abilities.

00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:10.670
Why wasn't I able to detect the 
presence of all of the enemies?

00:20:11.170 --> 00:20:12.430
You couldn't help it.

00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:15.260
I couldn't protect Gokotai.

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:18.990
What's more, I let Mikazuki 
get wounded like that.

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:24.700
I'm sure Master wanted to tell 
me that this is my true power.

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:28.860
I wonder if I'm hated now.

00:20:29.380 --> 00:20:30.360
Impossible.

00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:31.790
That's not it.

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:35.490
Mikazuki-san, you're finished 
with repairs, aren't you?

00:20:35.490 --> 00:20:38.030
Yes, I've been looked after well.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:41.560
May I join you?

00:20:41.990 --> 00:20:42.920
Yeah.

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:49.060
I was just delivering the battle 
progress report to Master.

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:54.010
There, I learned the reason that I was
 chosen for dispatch this time.

00:20:54.710 --> 00:21:00.240
It was because they wanted me 
to see how you fight, Kashuu.

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:07.070
Master praised your fighting for being 
extremely daring and dependable.

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:09.300
You are loved.

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:13.860
But I wasn't able to protect you or Gokotai.

00:21:14.190 --> 00:21:19.380
It is because you protected us, Kashuu, 
that I was able to go to Gokotai.

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:22.250
You even gave me a
chance to steal the show.

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:25.460
I may be an old man,
but I can be unexpectedly useful.

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:28.220
I wish I could have shown 
you, too, Yamatonokami.

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:31.690
I cannot remain a hindrance forever.

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:35.640
Kashuu, will you spar with me next time?

00:21:38.740 --> 00:21:39.780
Mikazuki.

00:21:41.490 --> 00:21:44.830
How can I become kinder, like you?

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:49.070
I do not know if I am kind.

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:52.030
Kindness is being able to 
properly see your opponent.

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:55.490
And being able to see your 
opponent is called strength.

00:21:55.830 --> 00:21:59.950
After seeing all the things that
 I have seen, that is what I think.

00:22:01.770 --> 00:22:03.870
Kindness is strength.

00:22:15.310 --> 00:22:17.480
You say that like an old man.

00:22:17.480 --> 00:22:19.120
Because I am an old man.

00:22:19.760 --> 00:22:21.870
Brilliant, brilliant.

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:59.990
<b>More Hanamaru Next Week!</b>
